        "id": 213306,
        "name": "WalkingTarget",
        "username": "WalkingTarget",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/walkingtarget/{size}/4833_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-10T21:03:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Christopher\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/48/1851_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Christopher:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\nAs a completely unbiased voice on the internet what is your opinion of Fate of the Elder Gods?\n</blockquote>\nI like it a bunch! It's a good game. I love all the ways the mechanics work together to support and advance the theme, and the individual powers for each god/cult/lodge are awesome. However! It is not so much for me, as a primary part of the game play is \"take that\" stuff that you do to other cults by sending investigators at them or cursing them, and I am not one for \"take that\" games. I mean, look, I'm kind of into cooperative games, right?&nbsp;But yeah, definitely a good game, even if not for me.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I agree on the ”take that” aspect, and but of all of the “Lovecraftian games where you’re&nbsp;playing on the side of the baddies” that I’ve tried out, I think this one gets the tone down the best (which is why I picked it up to complement the cooperative “good guy” games in my collection and haven’t picked up others). So many Lovecraftian (or “Lovecraftian”) things out there get the scale wrong and make things too crazy or too “epic”.</p>",
